<!-- One generated student chickadee.

     Rendered from an AvatarPresentation passed as a SUB-CONTEXT
     (Core/AvatarMarkup.swift), which carries palette TOKEN NAMES rather than
     colours and a wing symbol reference rather than any geometry.

     The sub-context form makes the passed object this partial's root, so its
     fields are addressed flat here. Qualifying them with the caller's field
     name yields empty strings, silently, and a bird with no colours and no
     wing still renders and still returns 200.

     The five use elements below are the whole bird, back to front; their
     symbols live in the avatar sprite partial, which the page must ALSO
     include - once per page, not once per bird. Forget it and the page still
     returns 200 and shows an empty circle; no guard can catch that.

     The style attribute is a list of custom-property assignments and nothing
     else, which is what keeps it inside the inline-style allowlist. The cheek
     token appears twice on purpose: the marks on a patterned wing take the
     cheek colour so a pattern reads against any cap family.

     Both branches below carry the SAME style attribute and differ only in how
     the bird is announced. Edit one and you must edit the other - the drift
     test counts each assignment twice for exactly that reason.

     A page shows a bird beside a handle or a name most of the time, in which
     case it is decorative and the text beside it carries the identity. Where
     the bird stands alone it must announce whose it is, which is what the
     labelled branch is for. The caller decides, because only the caller can
     see what is next to it. -->
#if(isLabelled):
<svg class="#(sizeClass)" viewBox="0 0 64 64" role="img" aria-label="#(label)"
     style="--av-cap: var(#(capToken)); --av-wing: var(#(wingToken)); --av-beak: var(#(beakToken)); --av-cheek: var(#(cheekToken)); --av-wing-mark: var(#(cheekToken)); --av-flank: var(#(flankToken)); --av-backdrop: var(#(backdropToken))">
#else:
<svg class="#(sizeClass)" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"
     style="--av-cap: var(#(capToken)); --av-wing: var(#(wingToken)); --av-beak: var(#(beakToken)); --av-cheek: var(#(cheekToken)); --av-wing-mark: var(#(cheekToken)); --av-flank: var(#(flankToken)); --av-backdrop: var(#(backdropToken))">
#endif
    <use href="#av-backdrop"/>
    <use href="#av-plumage"/>
    <use href="#(wingSymbolRef)"/>
    <use href="#av-beak"/>
    <use href="#av-eyes"/>
</svg>
